Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790330399999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The strongest counterargument is that the trend keeps producing spiking highs that are not held: bar 86 reached 2771 with a 255.70-point upper tail and was followed by 27 sideways bars, and bar 117 now shows the same shape with high 2850 and close 2775.61 (74.39-point tail), so the current 'breakout' may be another overshoot rather than a durable spike.", "Trading-range behaviour dominates the window: bars 11-35, 50-83 and 87-113 are three multi-week ranges covering roughly 86 of 120 bars, so this market has repeatedly reverted to range after every strong leg, which weakens a trend-continuation label.", "The pullback is large relative to the leg: 216.69 points (~7.6%) from 2850 to 2633.31 in only three bars, and bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts the low 2641.70 of the breakout bar 117, a sign that the spike's momentum is already being absorbed.", "The last 20 bars are only net +207 (bar 101 close 2479.28 to bar 120 close 2686.59) while containing both a new high 2850 and a deep dip to 2358.62 (bar 111), i.e., two-sided rather than one-directional pressure."], "evidence_for": ["Acceptance above a multi-week range: four consecutive closes (2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, 2775.61) above the 2557.46 top of the 27-bar bars 87-113 range, with a new window high at 2850 (bar 117).", "Swing progression is upward across the window: higher lows 1368.42 -> 1512.91 -> 1803.74 -> 2357.18 paired with higher highs 1944.39 -> 1974.46 -> 2771 -> 2850.", "The pullback after the breakout is being bought above the breakout level: bars 118-120 hold low 2633.31, and bar 120 closes 2686.59, 129 points above 2557.46 and in the upper 81% of its own 66.08 range.", "The 27-bar range (bars 87-113) resolved upward with follow-through bars 115 and 116 (closes 2632.98 and 2642.90) rather than immediately reversing, unlike the failed bar 61 (1974.46) and bar 107 (2680) probes inside earlier ranges."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window covers 120 closed D1 bars from open 1779926400000 to the final close 1790294399999; window low is 1368.42 (bar 10, close 1780790399999) and window high is 2850 (bar 117, close 1789948800000), a 108% advance from low to high.", "Bars 6-10 are five consecutive lower closes (1859.02, 1813.04, 1731.00, 1581.32, 1568.55), breaking the bars 1-5 range of 1958.77-2042.37; bar 6 opens 2006.06 with high 2006.17 and closes 1859.02.", "Bar 10 prints the window low 1368.42 but closes 1568.55, a 200.13-point lower tail (87% of its 230.85 range) - a climactic reversal bar rather than a clean bear trend bar.", "Bars 11-35 are two-sided and overlapping between high 1845.09 (bar 19) and low 1512.91 (bar 30); bar 30's 1512.91 is a higher low versus 1368.42.", "Bars 36-49 rally from 1597.72 (bar 36 low) to 1944.39 (bar 49 high) with consecutive bull closes 1889.93 and 1917.02 (bars 48-49).", "Bars 50-83 form a 34-bar overlapping range between 1803.74 (bar 51 low) and 1974.46 (bar 61 high); bar 61 opens 1953.92, tags 1974.46 and closes 1891.41, and bars 73 and 80 have ranges of only 13.24 and 10.41 (doji cluster).", "Bars 84-86 are a bull spike: bar 84 opens 1916.51 with low 1905.63 and closes 2252.16; bar 86 prints high 2771 but closes 2515.30, leaving a 255.70-point upper tail.", "Bars 87-113 hold a 27-bar range between 2357.18 (bar 98 low) and 2557.46 (bar 92 high); bar 107 spikes to 2680 and closes 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 114-117 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61, all above the 2557.46 range high, and bar 117 reaches the new window high 2850.", "Bars 118-120 pull back from bar 118 high 2776.18 to bar 120 low 2633.31; bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts bar 117's low 2641.70, and bar 120 closes 2686.59 (81% of its 66.08 range) still 129 points above the 2557.46 breakout level."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bear breakout of the bars 1-5 range 1958.77-2042.37, with five consecutive bear closes down to the 1368.42 low; bar 6 opens 2006.06 and closes 1859.02, bar 10 closes 1568.55.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780358400000, "upper_boundary": "2042.37"}, {"description": "Sell-climax reversal bar at the 1368.42 low: close 1568.55 with a 200.13-point lower tail, ending the bear spike and starting the basing process.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780704000000, "upper_boundary": "1599.27"}, {"description": "Post-spike two-sided range with heavy overlap and alternating closes; high 1845.09 (bar 19), higher low 1512.91 (bar 30), roughly 1500-1850 area.", "end_time_ms": 1783036799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the 1597.72 low (bar 36) to the 1944.39 high (bar 49), continued by a pullback low of 1803.74 (bar 51).", "end_time_ms": 1784073599999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "1597.72", "start_time_ms": 1782950400000, "upper_boundary": "1944.39"}, {"description": "34-bar overlapping range between 1803.74 (bar 51 low) and 1974.46 (bar 61 high); the bar 61 probe above 1974.46 failed and closed 1891.41, and bars 73 and 80 are very small doji bars.", "end_time_ms": 1787097600000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1803.74", "start_time_ms": 1784160000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the 1800-1975 range: bar 84 rises from 1916.51 to close 2252.16, and bar 86 spikes to 2771 before closing 2515.30 (buy climax with a 255.70-point upper tail).", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "27-bar range after the spike between 2357.18 (bar 98 low) and 2557.46 (bar 92 high); bar 107 overshoots to 2680 but closes 2514.72 back inside the range.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2557.46"}, {"description": "Four-bar breakout above the 2557.46 range top: closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61, with bar 117 printing the window high 2850 (74.39-point upper tail).", "end_time_ms": 1789948800000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Three-bar pullback from bar 118 high 2776.18 to bar 120 low 2633.31 that holds above the 2557.46 breakout level; bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts bar 117's low 2641.70 and bar 120 closes 2686.59 near the top of its range.", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2776.18"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Two or more consecutive closes above 2776.18 (bar 118 high) would confirm the bars 114-117 leg as a continuing spike and keep the read as bull breakout.", "A daily close back below 2557.46 (the bars 87-113 range top) would mark the breakout as failed and revert the primary read to trading-range with an upper boundary near 2850.", "A close below bar 120's low 2633.31 followed by a lower high below 2776.18 would shift the always-in to short and raise the higher-high MTR-like interpretation of 2771 versus 2850.", "Continued overlapping closes between roughly 2633 and 2776 with small bodies would move the phase from breakout-spike toward channel or range without changing the bullish regime label."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790323199999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The last 24 bars are two-sided: swing highs step down from 2850 to 2804.59, 2786.81, then 2699.53/2699.39, and bar 1790164800000 broke the 2716.01 range floor with a large bear bar closing at 2659.", "The 2850 bar closed 127 points off its high and later bars could not exceed 2804.59 despite two 2700 tests, i.e. a failed upside breakout after a climax-type bar.", "The final 10 bars overlap heavily between 2633.31 and 2699.53 with small bodies and the last bar closing in the lower third of its range, which is trading-range behavior, not trend continuation.", "The first roughly 62 bars traded inside a 2358.62-2680 range including a failed spike to 2680, so over half the window is two-sided and a single-direction trend label is only partially descriptive."], "evidence_for": ["Second half of the window has a clear higher-high/higher-low sequence (highs 2643.52, 2700, 2850; lows 2358.62, 2569.8, 2633.31) with the 2850 pullback holding above the 2569.8 swing low.", "Repeated strong bull bars closing near their highs (1789128000000 close 2555.52; 1789732800000 close 2578.6; 1789747200000 close 2636.28; 1789977600000 close 2723.15) show directional demand rather than one isolated spike.", "The 2850 pullback low 2633.31 stops above the early-range top zone (2607.62/2609.02/2680), so the decline reads as a test of the prior breakout area, a common bull-flag location.", "The last bar closes at 2671.19, about 13.2% above the window low 2358.62 and inside the upper half of the window's 2358.62-2850 span."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["The 120-bar window opened at 2452.6 and closed at 2671.19; it first traded a two-sided range capped by 2528.8 (bar 1788739200000) and floored near 2411.04 (bar 1789041600000), spiked to 2680 on bar 1789128000000, then fell to 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000) before rallying to a 2850 high (bar 1789977600000).", "The 2850 bar (open 2658.81, high 2850, close 2723.15) left a 127-point upper tail and the next bar made a lower high of 2795, so the push above the later 2804.59 high was rejected.", "Swing highs since that high decline (2850, 2804.59 on bar 1790020800000, 2786.81 on bar 1790136000000, then 2699.53/2699.39/2683.74), while swing lows stay higher (2358.62, 2569.8 on bar 1789862400000, 2633.31 on bar 1790236800000).", "Bar 1790164800000 was a large bear bar (open 2726.71, low 2648.49, close 2659) that broke the 2716.01 floor of the 2716.01-2804.59 range, but the next bar (open 2658.15, high 2681.21, close 2676.47) recovered most of it, so the downside break had no follow-through.", "The final 10 bars overlap heavily inside a 2633.31-2699.53 band; the last bar (open 2677.28, high 2683.74, low 2667.22, close 2671.19) closed in the lower third of a small range.", "Current price 2671.19 sits in the 2607.62/2609.02-2680 zone, the upper boundary of the early-window range, i.e. the pullback is testing the prior breakout area rather than the middle of the old range."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Early-window two-sided range: highs capped at 2528.8 and 2527.29 with repeated pushes above 2500 rejected, lows held near 2411.04; roughly 30 overlapping bars with no side achieving acceptance.", "end_time_ms": 1789113600000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2411.04", "start_time_ms": 1788667200000, "upper_boundary": "2528.8"}, {"description": "Single-bar spike on bar 1789128000000 from 2457.12 to 2680 (close 2555.52) that cleared the early range, but follow-through failed and price returned to 2358.62 within about 25 bars.", "end_time_ms": 1789488000000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789128000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the 2358.62 low to 2850: higher lows 2358.62, 2569.8, 2633.31 and higher highs 2643.52, 2700, 2850, built from strong bull bars such as 1789732800000 (close 2578.6), 1789747200000 (close 2636.28) and 1789977600000 (close 2723.15).", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Buy-climax candidate: bar 1789977600000 is the largest-range bar of the late window (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) at the end of a 34-bar bull run; it closes 127 points below its high and the following bar makes a lower high at 2795.", "end_time_ms": 1789992000000, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "2658.06", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Post-high trading range: about 13 bars between 2716.01 and 2804.59 with overlapping bodies, then a break below to 2648.49/2633.31 followed by a recovery; the last 10 bars trade 2633.31-2699.53 with no boundary acceptance on either side.", "end_time_ms": 1790323199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Possible major-trend-reversal setup: spike high 2850, lower high 2804.59, break of the 2716.01 range floor by bar 1790164800000, but no lower low below 2569.8 and no downside follow-through; reversal is suggested, not established.", "end_time_ms": null, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": null, "upper_boundary": null}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Acceptance above the 2786.81 high with follow-through (close above it and a hold) would support the bull trend resuming and put 2804.59 and 2850 back in play.", "A close below 2633.31 and then below 2607.62 would put price back inside the early range and shift the read toward a bear leg or range extension.", "Continued overlap with closes inside 2633-2700 without a boundary break keeps the trading-range phase and low Always-In relevance.", "A lower high below 2804.59 combined with a